Article 1 | Definitions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. "Project" means the overall contents of the DH_Tool_JA repository and its official releases, including the Licensed Material, integrated general-purpose third-party open-source components, and related materials involved, referenced, or accompanied for technical compatibility and community ecosystem interoperability.

2. "Licensed Material" means the source code, scripts, documentation, and resulting build outputs in the Project independently developed by the maintainer and contributors and separable from Third-Party Materials. This License grants rights in the Licensed Material only.

3. "Original Game and Related Commercial Assets" means together:
   (a) Original Game Assets: "Dread Hunger" and its official original assets (official artwork, audio, official code, trademarks, copyright-protected original asset data, etc.); and
   (b) Paid Commercial UE4 Assets: the paid commercial Unreal Engine 4 (UE4) assets contained in the game.

4. "Derived Files" means files created without authorization from the Lawful Rightsholders by modifying, extracting, or repacking Original Game and Related Commercial Assets, or files inseparable from them because they contain their content (such as modified or repacked .pak or .uasset files), regardless of author. Under this License, the test is whether the file contains such asset content; merely depending on or interacting with the game at run time is not "inseparable". Whether a file is an infringing derivative work by law depends on local applicable law.

5. "Independent Work" means a work written independently that contains no Licensed Material and no Original Game and Related Commercial Assets (such as an independent MOD script, plugin, or config). It remains an Independent Work even if loaded by this Project, calling or hooking game functions at run time, or using objective technical facts like memory offsets, parameter definitions, or interfaces. It is not subject to Articles 4 and 5, and copyright in its original expression belongs to its author. Mixed packages containing both Independent Works and Licensed Material or Derived Files are assessed part by part. Whether an Independent Work infringes statutory rights of Lawful Rightsholders is its author's own responsibility.

6. "Third-Party Materials" means Original Game and Related Commercial Assets, Derived Files, other independently developed community content not part of the Licensed Material, and general-purpose third-party open-source components unrelated to "Dread Hunger".

7. "Modified Version" means a work containing or adapting any copyright-protected part of the Licensed Material. An Independent Work is not a Modified Version.

8. "Distribute" means providing a copy of the Project or a Modified Version to anyone else by any means, including uploading, publishing, group sharing, or bundling with other content.

9. "Publicly Operate" means running a Modified Version as a game server open to players at large, or recruiting players via communities, groups, platforms, server lists, or similar channels. Private sessions and tests limited to you and acquaintances you directly invite, with no public recruitment, are not Public Operation.

10. "Corresponding Source" means all source code, scripts, and build configuration needed to build, install, and run a Modified Version, in original editable form (not obfuscated, encrypted, or compiled-only). It excludes Third-Party Materials and general build tools.

